From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:50:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 108/159] [ae-patch] Show Claude model versions and a Previous
 models list in both pickers

Reid asked for the Claude model menus to name versions ("Opus 5.5",
"Fable 5.1") instead of bare family names, and to reach every older Claude
model his subscription still serves, both in the new-chat harness picker and
in an open chat's model menu.

A Claude subscription's catalog lists only the newest model of each family,
under an alias ("opus" runs claude-opus-5-5), so the older ids come from a
static list in web/src/lib/aeClaudeModels.ts. Each id on it answered a
one-turn prompt on this subscription on 2026-10-19. Rows from Databricks,
gateways and inference config pass through unchanged; alias ids stay, so
the Default marker and the per-host caches keep matching. A picked older
row launches with its full id, which Claude Code accepts on a subscription.

The new-chat picker moves the older rows into a "Previous models" submenu
through a new trailing slot on a ComposerConfigSections section. The
session menu already routed older versions into a submenu that stayed
empty; it now receives the older rows and is titled "Previous models" for
Claude. Its version parser is shared with the new module, which also stops
a dated id such as claude-opus-4-20250514 reading its date as the minor
version.
